# /etc/shells - the login shells on this system.
#
# The list of shells a user may legitimately be given.  chsh(1) refuses a shell
# that is not here, ftp daemons reject logins whose shell is missing from it,
# and xterm consults it to decide whether the shell it is about to run is a
# real login shell -- if the file is absent, xterm falls back to /bin/sh
# regardless of what the password database says.
#
# One absolute path per line; lines starting with # are comments.

/bin/sh
/bin/bash
